  "subtitle": "A game controller with a thumb-driven spinning 'speed roller' for continuous analog speed input — alongside a joystick, four trigger buttons, and a numeric keypad.",
  "why_scout_cares": "The Super Action Controller is the museum's only hand-held game controller with a continuously-rotating analog 'speed roller' — an analog proportional input in an era when nearly every home controller was a digital switch. Spinning the roller for speed (racing, punch timing) is a distinct interaction grammar from every other controller in the collection (digital D-pads, ball joysticks, trackballs-as-pointing, touch plates).",
